; knowsia.com — Cloudflare import draft, compiled 2026-09-04 from live DNS lookups.
; Doc 20 (Domain Consolidation) Phase 0. Import via Cloudflare → DNS → Import and Export → Import.
;
; HOW THIS WAS BUILT: every record below was observed by querying the current authoritative
; servers (ns1/ns2.knowsia.com on the VPS). TXT lookups against those servers TIME OUT, so
; SPF / DKIM / DMARC could not be read — copy them from CyberPanel → DNS → knowsia.com before
; importing, or mail deliverability drops the moment the nameservers change. Everything marked
; VERIFY must be checked in CyberPanel's zone as well; anything present there and absent here
; must be added.
;
; TTLs are deliberately short (300 s) for the migration window. Raise to 3600 once stable.
;
; Cloudflare proxy status: import with DNS-only (grey cloud) for EVERY record. Vercel and
; the mail host need direct connections; the orange-cloud proxy in front of Vercel breaks TLS
; and caching assumptions.

$ORIGIN knowsia.com.
$TTL 300

; ---------- Apex and www (TODAY: WordPress on the VPS) ----------
; Phase 3 changes these two lines to:  @ A 76.76.21.21   and   www CNAME cname.vercel-dns.com.
@                 300  IN  A      64.20.36.232
www               300  IN  CNAME  knowsia.com.

; ---------- Mail (on the VPS — CyberPanel / Roundcube). Must move before Phase 4 ----------
@                 300  IN  MX 10  knowsia.com.
mail              300  IN  A      64.20.36.232
; VERIFY and paste from CyberPanel DNS (could not be read remotely):
; @                 300  IN  TXT    "v=spf1 a mx ip4:64.20.36.232 ~all"
; default._domainkey 300 IN  TXT    "v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=..."
; _dmarc            300  IN  TXT    "v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:info@knowsia.com"

; ---------- Applications ----------
reg               300  IN  CNAME  da623ee62209f472.vercel-dns-017.com.
; quiz.knowsia.com is BROKEN as of 2026-09-04: https://quiz.knowsia.com/ answers
; 301 to itself (a redirect loop) while https://knowsia-quiz-app.web.app/ is
; fine. A bare CNAME to the web.app host is not how Firebase Hosting custom
; domains work — the domain has to be added in the Firebase console
; (Hosting → Add custom domain), which issues a TXT verification record and
; two A records (Firebase's anycast IPs) to use INSTEAD of this CNAME. Keep the
; line below only until that is done, then replace it with what the console gives.
quiz              300  IN  CNAME  knowsia-quiz-app.web.app.
; Phase 1 adds:
; app               300  IN  CNAME  cname.vercel-dns.com.
; Phase 3 adds (VPS kept reachable for 60–90 days, noindex):
; legacy            300  IN  A      64.20.36.232

; ---------- Legacy hosting conveniences (VPS) ----------
ftp               300  IN  CNAME  knowsia.com.

; ---------- Nameserver glue (drop once Cloudflare is authoritative) ----------
; ns1 / ns2.knowsia.com currently point at the VPS. After the registrar switch these are unused;
; keep them for 7 days in case anything cached still asks, then delete.
ns1               300  IN  A      64.20.36.232
ns2               300  IN  A      64.20.36.232

; ---------- Verification records ----------
; Vercel domain verification for knowsia.com (Vercel → course-registration → Domains shows the
; exact TXT name/value when you add the domain):
; _vercel           300  IN  TXT    "vc-domain-verify=knowsia.com,..."
; Google Search Console domain property (Search Console → Add property → Domain shows the value):
; @                 300  IN  TXT    "google-site-verification=..."
